@startuml
title Assign Role To User Sequence (/api/superadmin/roles/{roleId}/users/{userId})
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor SuperAdmin
boundary "Role Assignment UI" as RoleAssignmentPage
control "AdminAccountsController\n(FE Dashboard)" as DashboardController
entity "AdminUserSummary\n(FE Response DTO)" as FeUserDto
entity "ManagedRole\n(FE Response DTO)" as FeRoleDto
control "AdminUsersController\n(BE API)" as AdminUsersController
control "RolesController\n(BE API)" as ApiController
control "IRoleManagementService" as IRoleManagementService
control "RoleManagementService" as RoleService
entity "Role" as RoleEntity
entity "User" as UserEntity
entity "RefreshToken" as RefreshTokenEntity
control "IRoleManagementRepository" as IRoleManagementRepository
control "RoleManagementRepository" as RoleRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL
note over RoleAssignmentPage, MySQL
Checked in current code:
Dashboard AdminAccountsController handles role assignment.
VocaNovaApiClient calls POST /api/superadmin/roles/{roleId}/users/{userId}.
FE response DTOs exist: AdminUserSummary and ManagedRole for loading assignable data.
No request DTO body is used; API returns bool in the response envelope.
Assigning a role revokes active refresh tokens for the user.
Interfaces used in code: IRoleManagementService, IRoleManagementRepository.
end note
SuperAdmin -> RoleAssignmentPage: Open role assignment page
RoleAssignmentPage -> DashboardController: GET /admin-accounts/role-assignment(search, role, page)
DashboardController -> AdminUsersController: VocaNovaApiClient.GetUsersAsync(filter)\nGET /api/admin/users(role filter)
AdminUsersController -> FeUserDto: HTTP 200 OK\nPaged AdminUserSummary JSON
FeUserDto --> DashboardController: Paged users
DashboardController --> RoleAssignmentPage: Render assignable users
SuperAdmin -> RoleAssignmentPage: Select target role
RoleAssignmentPage -> DashboardController: POST /admin-accounts/{id}/role
DashboardController -> DashboardController: Validate role value(user or admin)
alt Role input invalid
DashboardController --> RoleAssignmentPage: Show error message
else Role input valid
DashboardController -> ApiController: VocaNovaApiClient.GetRolesAsync()\nGET /api/superadmin/roles
ApiController -> IRoleManagementService: GetRolesAsync(query)
IRoleManagementService -> RoleService: GetRolesAsync(query)
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: GetRolesAsync(query)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: GetRolesAsync(query)
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Query roles
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT roles
MySQL --> DbContext: Role rows
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role rows
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Roles
DbContext --> RoleRepository: Result
RoleRepository --> RoleService: Paged roles
RoleService --> ApiController: Return roles result
ApiController -> FeRoleDto: HTTP 200 OK\nPaged RoleResponse JSON
FeRoleDto --> DashboardController: Paged ManagedRole
alt Target role not found
DashboardController --> RoleAssignmentPage: Show error message
else Target role found
DashboardController -> ApiController: VocaNovaApiClient.AssignRoleAsync(roleId, userId)\nPOST /api/superadmin/roles/{roleId}/users/{userId}
ApiController -> ApiController: Check super admin authorization
ApiController -> IRoleManagementService: AssignRoleAsync(roleId, userId)
IRoleManagementService -> RoleService: AssignRoleAsync(roleId, userId)
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: GetRoleNameAsync(roleId)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: GetRoleNameAsync(roleId)
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Query target role
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT roles
MySQL --> DbContext: Role row or null
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role?
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Role or null
DbContext --> RoleRepository: Result
RoleRepository --> RoleService: role name or null
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: GetUserRoleNameAsync(userId)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: GetUserRoleNameAsync(userId)
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Query current user role
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT user with role
MySQL --> DbContext: User row or null
DbContext -> UserEntity: Materialize User?
UserEntity --> DbContext: User or null
DbContext --> RoleRepository: Result
RoleRepository --> RoleService: user role name or null
alt Role/user not found or protected role
RoleService --> ApiController: NotFound/Forbidden result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 404/403 error
DashboardController --> RoleAssignmentPage: Show error message
else User already has this role
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: GetRoleIdByNameAsync(currentRole)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: GetRoleIdByNameAsync(currentRole)
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Query current role id
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT roles
MySQL --> DbContext: Role id
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Role
DbContext --> RoleRepository: Result
RoleRepository --> RoleService: current role id
RoleService --> ApiController: Conflict result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 409 error
DashboardController --> RoleAssignmentPage: Show error message
else Role can be assigned
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: GetRoleIdByNameAsync(currentRole)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: GetRoleIdByNameAsync(currentRole)
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Query current role id
DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT roles
MySQL --> DbContext: Role id
DbContext -> RoleEntity: Materialize Role
RoleEntity --> DbContext: Role
DbContext --> RoleRepository: Result
RoleRepository --> RoleService: current role id
RoleService -> IRoleManagementService: Begin transaction
IRoleManagementService -> RoleService: Begin transaction
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: AssignRoleAsync(roleId, userId)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: AssignRoleAsync(roleId, userId)
RoleRepository -> UserEntity: Set RoleId
UserEntity --> RoleRepository: User updated
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Track user role
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE users
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
RoleService -> IRoleManagementRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(userId)
IRoleManagementRepository -> RoleRepository: RevokeActiveRefreshTokensAsync(userId)
RoleRepository -> RefreshTokenEntity: Set RevokedAt
RefreshTokenEntity --> RoleRepository: RefreshToken updated
RoleRepository -> DbContext: Track refresh token updates
DbContext -> MySQL: UPDATE refresh_tokens
MySQL --> DbContext: Update result
DbContext --> RoleRepository: Save result
RoleRepository --> RoleService: Saved
RoleService --> ApiController: Success result
ApiController --> DashboardController: HTTP 200 OK
DashboardController --> RoleAssignmentPage: Show feedback and refresh page
end
end
end
@enduml
